From: polaris research
Subject: [PATCH] 0258: dipper-xnu a630 hw_init table behind sweetdipper=1

Replay dipper-xnu's 180-entry a630 hardware-init table in our driver: ADDRESS, HWCG (only
when RBBM_CLOCK_CNTL is not 0x8aa8aa02), HWCG_COMMIT, CORE, the GMU busy/power counters and
the whole PROTECT range, in dipper's order. SECVID and the IRQ entry stay out (zap owns
SECVID; our driver polls). Only with sweetdipper=1; the default kernel is unchanged.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_dipper_init.c
@@ -0,0 +1,292 @@
